1
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,240
Had not intended to become an officer, had not intended to be a pilot.

2
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,080
Now I'm all three.

3
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,040
There is a picture that pilots are some kind of über people.

4
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,440
We are not.

5
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:23,760
It's about being specific more than special.

6
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,120
One cliché that people say is "One day is not the same."

7
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,120
Here, weekdays are incredibly similar.

8
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,760
We follow the same routine.

9
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,520
It is weather brief, air traffic conductor review

10
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,560
Air pass and debrief.

11
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,760
What is good is the great contrasts between the weeks.

12
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,680
So there is a lot to read too.

13
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,680
The flight itself is quite unpublished

14
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,840
But we have to keep a good shape.

15
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,600
So training is a big part too.

16
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,040
Late obviously a sense of freedom

17
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,440
to get to rush forward

18
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,840
between cobbles and cuts

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,080
The sun sparkles and

20
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,560
You see the waves go a little.

21
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,240
It is also wonderful of course.

22
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:29,120
My name is Freddy and I am a helicopter pilot.
